The actual construction here is the same double-equilateral-triangle construction of the previous proposition that is used to bisect the line {DE}, except that it is preceded by the selection of points {D} and {E} on {AB} equidistant from {C}.

This construction actually only requires drawing three circles and the one line {FG|GF}.

#### Use of Proposition 11

This construction is used in propositions @I.13, @I.46, @I.48, and numerous propositions in Books II, III, VI, VI, XI, XII, and XIII.
